#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:2 ff6d45aaf3944906a37e7d8e04dbee95
msgid "When something is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:4 e10200e66c9b4cea8f65d69c2dd62b41
msgid "The usual causes, what each looks like, and the command that settles it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:11
#: c86a80a4185341b3977f0b3272ad5c29
msgid "Three answers that disagree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:13
#: d760e6ab2cf84b63ace3a85487ec9f14
msgid ""
"A drive's state can be asked three ways, and they do not always agree. "
"This is the single most confusing thing about MHVTL, and it is worth "
"knowing before it happens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:28
#: 71f83842365a4d1a8704a6bcf5e496f3
msgid ""
"That was a real drive with a real cartridge in it, which wrote and read "
"back perfectly. ``mt`` was simply stale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:31
#: 1fa8f99e94f94ca196863e2db91e18f2
msgid ""
"**Believe the robot and the daemon.** The robot moved the cartridge, the "
"daemon is holding it, and the daemon's counters are the only ones that "
"keep working during a backup - the kernel gives the SCSI reservation to "
"whoever is writing, and ``mt`` and ``mtx`` answer *device busy* until it "
"finishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:37
#: be01675653d44491b38a5d5c409bc05e
msgid "\"Restart the library for its robot to see this\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:39
#: 8ad2deeeb3814e728dfb1055653d3700
msgid ""
"MHVTL reads its configuration **once**, when a daemon starts. Adding a "
"tape, adopting one, or changing the slot count edits the file, and the "
"running robot knows nothing about it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:49
#: c774c391d90d46e582352f38d8131888
msgid ""
"Until you do, ``mhvtl tape list`` shows the new cartridge and ``mhvtl "
"status library`` does not. The console says the same on the library page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:57
#: 6c71095b29a548e6ac7da9f90bd2c513
msgid "A drive says ``silent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:59
#: b22d04b7c0904173a3ade3526eaa47d6
msgid ""
"Its daemon is not running. Nothing is broken about the library; that one "
"drive is simply absent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:75
#: 84ec8f92c4ff4c8eb021a7e56a98d6ce
msgid "A library page that answers 404"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:77
#: 10c3762c19944526a829600634d77ef8
msgid ""
"A library made from the command line exists in the configuration before "
"the console's database hears of it. Opening the page syncs it first, so "
"this should be rare. If it persists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:87
#: 7f315cf0631c4f70ab4d574aca4f44fc
msgid "An export that points at the wrong device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:89
#: efca90773f31411fa2e5242c40c435d8
msgid ""
"``/dev/sg`` numbers change when the MHVTL module reloads and when a "
"library is recreated. An iSCSI export remembers a node, so after either "
"it may be pointing at something else entirely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:101
#: c9b04a27e50248efa41470de90e9bfa1
msgid ""
"This runs at boot as well. The iSCSI page shows the same per device: "
"**Created on**, **Device now**, and whether they agree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:105
#: 50f2aeea1afb4f4f9478f42244e6f478
msgid "Tapes that belong to no library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:107
#: fa8e80246bd14b84aac3cb8f1b758052
msgid ""
"Removing a library leaves its cartridges on disk on purpose - they are "
"data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:120
#: 1d0b90d1aef54d5a9f20692b45040b78
msgid "See :doc:`../tapes/adopt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:123
#: aea50e03899c4220b6952ae2feb65fef
msgid "A drive that will not take a cartridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:125
#: 37edfec763ae40f7bcb865a8a4c7a121
msgid "Check that the drive writes that generation at all:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:131
#: 31d01a35a5764979a876c0ee6d044ee2
msgid ""
"A drive reads older cartridges and writes recent ones, as the real "
"hardware does. Mounting an LTO-5 cartridge into an LTO-8 drive is allowed"
" and reading it works; writing to it does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:136
#: 4ee15264e05b41c4a84ede874d18e14c
msgid "The disk is full"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:138
#: c16ead1621464dbfa80cdaceea6c6c9f
msgid ""
"Tapes are files, so a full disk fails writes in ways that look like drive"
" faults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:145
#: ecbbdff8703e4cb5adaf08ff1b807095
msgid ""
"A cartridge occupies only what has been written to it, so the problem is "
"usually one library that has had a great deal written to it, not the "
"number of cartridges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:150
#: bc8ed11f6c174f61b908e6761e6dcd5b
msgid "Removing a library and rebooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:152
#: 40de04fcab42408fa377743da74079f6
msgid ""
"On this host the kernel ``ch`` driver is blacklisted, because it takes a "
"reference on every drive a changer reports and never releases it - the "
"drives' SCSI addresses then stay unusable until a reboot. If a newly "
"created library is missing drives, or ``rmmod mhvtl`` says the module is "
"in use with everything stopped, read *The kernel ch driver leak* in the "
"*Guides*. Only a reboot clears it."
msgstr ""

